IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- THE PENSION INDEX (regulation 75).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 742 to 746.
--
-- For each year the Pension Index is the average of the Consumer Price Index for the twelve months ending October 31
-- of the preceding year, rounded to one digit after the decimal point by looking at the second digit (5 or more rounds
-- up). Section 43(2) of the Act (a Pension Index that falls is replaced by the earlier one, piece cp3) is not applied here.
-- The Consumer Price Index figures are published by Statistics Canada and are an input (the keel notes: they are data).

§ `Part V -- The Pension Index (regulation 75)`

-- src:743 | 75 (1) For the purposes of subsection 43(2) of the Act, the Pension Index for each year shall be calculated as the quotient obtained by dividing the aggregate of the Consumer Price Index for each month in the 12-month period ending October 31 in the preceding year by 12, adjusted to one digit after the decimal point in accordance with subsection (2).
-- src:744 | (2) Where the quotient obtained pursuant to subsection (1) contains a fraction that is less than one, that fraction shall be expressed as a decimal fraction of two digits after the decimal point and
-- src:745 | (a) the second digit after the decimal point shall be dropped if that digit is less than five; or
-- src:746 | (b) the first digit after the decimal point shall be increased by one and the second digit dropped if the second digit is five or greater than five.
@ref Reg 75(2) (src:744-746)
GIVEN quotient IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 75(2) — a quotient adjusted to one digit after the decimal point` quotient MEANS
    FLOOR ((quotient TIMES 10) PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 10

@ref Reg 75(1) (src:743)
GIVEN `the Consumer Price Index for each month in the 12-month period ending October 31 in the preceding year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 75(1) — the Pension Index for a year`
    `the Consumer Price Index for each month in the 12-month period ending October 31 in the preceding year` MEANS
    IF count `the Consumer Price Index for each month in the 12-month period ending October 31 in the preceding year` EQUALS 12
    THEN JUST (`reg 75(2) — a quotient adjusted to one digit after the decimal point`
                 ((sum `the Consumer Price Index for each month in the 12-month period ending October 31 in the preceding year`) DIVIDED BY 12))
    ELSE NOTHING
